  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Murnaghan-Nakayama rule for the cyclotomic Hecke algebra and applications — We establish a Murnaghan–Nakayama rule for the irreducible characters of the cyclotomic Hecke algebra Hm,n(q, u) on Shoji’s\n\n**Murnaghan-Nakayama rule for the cyclotomic Hecke algebra and applications**\n\n*NAIHUAN JING AND NING LIU*\n\n56 pp, 12 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We establish a Murnaghan–Nakayama rule for the irreducible characters of the cyclotomic Hecke algebra Hm,n(q, u) on Shoji’s standard elements. Combined with Shoji’s determinacy result, our formula provides a direct combinatorial route to the full irreducible character table of Hm,n(q, u). Our construction is based on our recent multi- parameter Murnaghan–Nakayama rule for Macdonald polynomials and specializes uni- formly to several previously known formulas, including those for the complex reflection group of type G(m, 1, n) and the Iwahori–Hecke algebras of types A and B. In a dual framework, using the vertex operator realization of Schur functions, we also derive a com- plementary iterative formula for irreducible characters on upper multipartitions, which may be viewed as a dual Murnaghan–Nakayama rule.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Preliminaries; 3 Murnaghan–Nakayama rule for the cyclotomic H; 4 Special cases of the Murnaghan–Nakayama rule; 5 A dual Murnaghan–Nakayama rule via vertex op; 6 Application I: Regev-type formula; 7 Application II: Lübeck–Prasad–Adin–Roichman-; 8 Multiple bitrace for the irreducible charact; Appendix A. An alternative proof of Corollary ; Appendix B. SageMath implementation of the Mur; References",
      "lang": "en",
